1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.buenosaires.gob.ar/sites/gcaba/files/anton_rudez_un_esloveno_en_el_lago_skadar.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT Anton Rudez, un esloveno en el lago Skadar en 1916, por Carlos Newland (carlosnewland@gmail.com) Lo que sé de mi bisabuelo Anton Rudez (1871-1932) lo escuché de boca de mi tía Catalina Zorc, quien lo conoció en su niñez. Además de
2 CONC  recuerdos, mi tía conserva fotos familiares, algunas de las cuales están relacionadas con la Primera Guerra Mundial y que aquí se incluyen. Anton era el primogénito de una familia terrateniente de Ribnica, Eslovenia, en ese enton
2 CONC ces parte del Imperio Austro Húngaro. En 1901 había recibido de su padre la gestión de los bosques y tierras familiares, actividad a la que dedicó su vida, junto con la administración de su aserradero. Había realizado estudios de 
2 CONC Ingeniería forestal en Viena, y como todo universitario, le correspondía desempeñarse como oficial de reserva del Ejército Austríaco.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.researchgate.net/publication/329247105_Lords_of_the_ribnica_manor_Anton_rudez_sr_and_Anton_rudez_jr_as_the_last_patrons_of_the_parish_of_sodrazica
2 CONT
2 CONT Lords of the ribnica manor Anton rudež sr. and Anton rudež jr. as the last patrons of the parish of sodražica Article in Kronika (Ljubljana, Slovenia) 66(3):625-638 · January 2018 with 9 Reads  Cite this publication M. Ambrožič
2 CONT
2 CONT Abstract
2 CONT
2 CONT Ribnica seigniory exercised the rights of patronage over the parish vicariate of Sodražica since its founding in 1753 and over the parish itself in the period of 1862-1936. Initially, the rights of patronage were exercised by its 
2 CONC owners, the Counts of Kobenzl, and from 1810 onwards by the lords of the Ribnica's manor, the Rudež family. The patronage rights became a point of dispute in 1936, when the patron, engineer Anton Rudež Jr., sold the Ribnica manor 
2 CONC and part of the large estate to the military treasury, claiming that he was no longer the patron, because this would oblige him to co-fund the restoration works on parish buildings in Sodražica. However, the military treasury refu
2 CONC sed to shoulder the burden of patronage as well, having bought the manor and the estate free of debt. The controversy led to a lengthy legal dispute, which never reached a closing epilogue. © 2018 Zveza Zgodovinskih Drustev Sloven
2 CONC ije. All Rights Reserved.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Updated from [http://www.myheritage.com/research/collection-1/myheritage-family-trees?itemId=193869301-2-142156&action=showRecord&indId=externalindividual-b9e09a398b2035af0d6fa104e04f07e5&mrid=19197300cd93993cc3eca4068e577b11 My
2 CONC Heritage Family Trees] via father [http://www.geni.com/profile-34673411254 Teodor Bernard Rudež] by [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jun 19 2015, 11:52:43 UTC''
