1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Anna Pessiak-Schmerling (1834 – 14 March 1896) was an Austrian composer born in Vienna. She was the granddaughter of Giannatasio del Rio, and studied with Madame Marchesi. She worked as a professor of voice at the 
2 CONC Conservatory in Vienna. She composed piano work and songs, and was noted for her masses and other sacred works. ([http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anna_Pessiak-Schmerling Wikipedia])
