1 NAME Hertha Hedwig Paula Louise /Stölzle/
2 GIVN Hertha Hedwig Paula Louise
2 SURN Stölzle
2 _MARNM Hay (Biheller, Willfort)
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 3 JUN 1902
2 PLAC Alt-Nagelberg
2 ADDR
3 CITY Nagelberg
3 STAE Niederösterreich
3 CTRY Austria
1 DEAT
2 DATE 27 JAN 1994
2 ADDR
3 CITY London
3 STAE England
3 CTRY United Kingdom
1 OCCU 1940 Women's Auxiliary Royal Air Force
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Hertha Hedwig Paula Louise, divorced HAY, widowed BIHELLER, divorced WILLFORT, née STÖLZLE: b. 3 June 1902, Alt-Nagelberg - d. 27 Jan 1994, London
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1940 Hertha was a member of the Women's Auxiliary Royal Air Force.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hertha was married several times.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1st. marriage: cousin Emil MAYER-STÖLZLE, 1920
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage not recognised by church.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2nd. marriage: Felix WILLFORT, 1921
2 CONT
2 CONT Son born 1922. Divorced before 1927.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3rd. marriage: Walter BIHELLER, 1927, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Walter died in 1932
2 CONT
2 CONT N.B. Simon BIHELLER had a firm called "WEISS & BIHELLER", located at 70 & 71, Chiswell St., London EC, and, for a certain period, "BROOKS, WEISS & BIHELLER",
2 CONT
2 CONT This company was known as a glass & china merchant. They also acted as U.K. agents for STÖLZLE glass products. (cf. advertisement shown under "Media"). It is likely that Hertha STÖLZLE met Walter BIHELLER via this business connect
2 CONC ion.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4th. marriage: Sir Arthur Thomas Errol HAY of Park, 4 March 1935, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Son born 1935. Divorced 1942.
2 CONT
2 CONT Information from numerous sources including the following:
2 CONT
2 CONT The delusions of Walter Biheller | Great War London
2 CONT
2 CONT https://greatwarlondon.wordpress.com/2013/04/06/the-delusions-of-walter-biheller/ 
2 CONT
2 CONT "A few bits of information about Biheller emerge from the years after 1919, though. In the 1920s, he lived with his parents at 19 Frognal Lane, Hampstead. In 1927, he married fellow an Austrian-born woman named Hertha Hedwig Paula
2 CONC  Louise Stölzle (see p. 5 of this pdf). In the early 1930s, the couple are recorded as living at 5 Albert Terrace, Regent’s Park (next to Primrose Hill). When his father died in Germany in 1932, he inherited the family’s commercia
2 CONC l property at 70-71 Chiswell Street, Finsbury. Not long afterwards, though, Walter Biheller died – on 27 December 1932 at the German Hospital in Dalston. How he died, and whether it was linked to his illness, is not clear. Hertha 
2 CONC remarried a few years later and lived until the 1990s."
2 CONT
2 CONT And also ...
2 CONT
2 CONT Person Page 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p43506.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Arthur Thomas Erroll Hay of Park, 10th Bt.1
2 CONT
2 CONT M, #435052, b. 13 April 1909, d. 3 February 1993
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=15 Jan 2012
2 CONT
2 CONT      Sir Arthur Thomas Erroll Hay of Park, 10th Bt. was born on 13 April 1909.1 He was the son of Sir Lewis John Erroll Hay of Park, 9th Bt. and Lizabel Annie Macdonald.1 He married, firstly, Hertha Hedwig Paula Louise Stölzle, da
2 CONC ughter of Ludwig Stölzle, on 4 March 1935.1 He and Hertha Hedwig Paula Louise Stölzle were divorced in 1942.1 He married, secondly, Rosemary Evelyn Anne Lambert, daughter of Vice-Admiral Audrey Lambert, on 22 December 1942.1 He di
2 CONC ed on 3 February 1993 at age 83.1
2 CONT
2 CONT      He was educated at Fettes College, Edinburgh, Midlothian, ScotlandG.1 He succeeded as the 10th Baronet Hay, of Park [N.S., 1663] on 14 May 1923.1 He was registered as a Associate, Royal institute of British Architects (A.R.I.
2 CONC B.A.)1 He was awarded the Imperial Service Order (I.S.O.) circa 1970.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Sir Arthur Thomas Erroll Hay of Park, 10th Bt. and Hertha Hedwig Paula Louise Stölzle 1.	Sir John Erroll Audley Hay of Park, 11th Bt.2 b. 3 Dec 1935
2 CONT
2 CONT Significant details courtesy of:
2 CONT
2 CONT [PDF]Stammbaum Stölzle 1759 - aktuell - Pressglas-Korrespondenz
